1
00:00:08,934 --> 00:00:11,912
Oh, I love it!

2
00:00:11,912 --> 00:00:17,312
I love it!

3
00:00:17,312 --> 00:00:34,558
To be away from the city on such a beautiful day

4
00:00:34,558 --> 00:00:36,344
is my idea of heaven!

5
00:00:36,344 --> 00:01:05,515
The grass. The trees. The fresh air.

6
00:01:05,515 --> 00:01:12,471
I told you you'd like it. I've been doing this for years.

7
00:01:12,471 --> 00:01:20,405
You have the spirit of a teenager, Susan.

8
00:01:20,405 --> 00:01:25,133
Wait till you see yourself jumping around.

9
00:01:25,133 --> 00:01:30,799
That's what I love about Susan.

10
00:01:30,799 --> 00:01:32,317
She works hard.

11
00:01:32,317 --> 00:01:33,597
She plays hard.

12
00:01:33,597 --> 00:01:34,877
She's a real Stewart.

13
00:01:34,877 --> 00:01:36,271
Come on, Richard.

14
00:01:36,271 --> 00:01:38,656
Help me get this stuff out of the car.

15
00:01:38,656 --> 00:01:40,187
Where does it go?

16
00:01:40,187 --> 00:01:44,229
Well, we'll put everything over there.

17
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:47,207
We'll set up our tents over there by the edge of the woods.

18
00:01:47,207 --> 00:01:49,710
Then we'll be able to make our fire there where it's safe.

19
00:01:49,710 --> 00:01:51,401
Oh, there's our table and benches.

20
00:01:51,401 --> 00:01:52,617
All set for eating.

21
00:01:52,617 --> 00:01:59,118
That's what makes this spot so good.

22
00:01:59,118 --> 00:02:02,096
Is anybody hungry?

23
00:02:02,096 --> 00:02:03,096
I am.

24
00:02:03,096 --> 00:02:05,074
We just got here.

25
00:02:05,074 --> 00:02:08,385
When you're out in the fresh air like this, it makes you hungry.

26
00:02:08,385 --> 00:02:09,552
Aren't you hungry, Marilyn?

27
00:02:09,552 --> 00:02:10,552
I sure am.

28
00:02:10,552 --> 00:02:11,750
How about you, Richard?

29
00:02:11,750 --> 00:02:11,990
Starving.

30
00:02:11,990 --> 00:02:14,008
You guys are like three kids.

31
00:02:14,008 --> 00:02:16,986
Aren't you hungry, Harry?

32
00:02:16,986 --> 00:02:17,409
Well, yeah.

33
00:02:17,409 --> 00:02:19,312
Now that you mention it, I guess I am.

34
00:02:19,312 --> 00:02:19,735
I mean,

35
00:02:19,735 --> 00:02:22,942
how could a guy not be hungry with all this talk about eating?

36
00:02:22,942 --> 00:02:25,310
Where's the bag with the chicken salad sandwiches?

37
00:02:25,310 --> 00:02:28,170
Right here, next to the ice packs. Here.

38
00:02:28,170 --> 00:02:31,238
Put the tablecloth on the picnic table,

39
00:02:31,238 --> 00:02:34,854
and I will bring the cola and the plastic cups.

40
00:02:34,854 --> 00:02:38,832
Well, how do you like it so far?

41
00:02:38,832 --> 00:02:41,310
I've never been more relaxed.

42
00:02:41,310 --> 00:02:42,143
Me, neither.

43
00:02:42,143 --> 00:02:44,588
I wish we had brought Michelle, Harry.

44
00:02:44,588 --> 00:02:48,172
She would have loved it.

45
00:02:48,172 --> 00:02:50,280
Oh, you're right.

46
00:02:50,280 --> 00:02:53,568
I wish we had brought Max.

47
00:02:53,568 --> 00:02:57,687
Marilyn, Susan, let's not begin to worry about Michelle and Max. Marilyn Susan

48
00:02:57,687 --> 00:03:00,678
We're having a good time, and they're in good hands.

49
00:03:00,678 --> 00:03:01,345
Richard is right. Richard

50
00:03:01,345 --> 00:03:04,056
Are you having a good time, Susan?

51
00:03:04,056 --> 00:03:04,634
You haven't answered my question.

52
00:03:04,634 --> 00:03:08,354
I am having a good time, Harry.

53
00:03:08,354 --> 00:03:10,589
I promise not to think about the city.

54
00:03:10,589 --> 00:03:12,303
We're in the country.

55
00:03:12,303 --> 00:03:15,567
Let's all just enjoy this wonderful place

56
00:03:15,567 --> 00:03:38,677
and this wonderful weather.

57
00:03:38,677 --> 00:03:39,105
Good.

58
00:03:39,105 --> 00:03:40,625
This is heaven, Harry!

59
00:03:40,625 --> 00:03:44,633
It was such a great idea to spend the weekend this way.

60
00:03:44,633 --> 00:03:45,490
Thanks, Susan.

61
00:03:45,490 --> 00:03:47,658
I thought you'd all like it.

62
00:03:47,658 --> 00:03:49,303
Like it?

63
00:03:49,303 --> 00:03:53,614
Listen to the sounds of the summer that surround us.

64
00:03:53,614 --> 00:03:58,237
It's so calming.

65
00:03:58,237 --> 00:04:02,615
I've always liked camping out.

66
00:04:02,615 --> 00:04:06,250
Away from the telephones and account books.

67
00:04:06,250 --> 00:04:07,171
It's refreshing for me.

68
00:04:07,171 --> 00:04:11,989
I always go back to the city in a wonderful state of mind.

69
00:04:11,989 --> 00:04:14,879
We've only been here for a day,

70
00:04:14,879 --> 00:04:18,105
and I've completely forgotten about all my business problems.

71
00:04:18,105 --> 00:04:22,060
The office seems so far away.

72
00:04:22,060 --> 00:04:24,260
I'm glad you like it, Susan.

73
00:04:24,260 --> 00:04:26,718
We'll spend many more weekends like this.

74
00:04:26,718 --> 00:04:28,016
And next time we'll bring Michelle.

75
00:04:28,016 --> 00:04:33,972
I wish she were here with us to enjoy the country.

76
00:04:33,972 --> 00:04:39,928
And next time we'll bring Michelle.

77
00:04:39,928 --> 00:04:43,906
Just listen to the sound.

78
00:04:43,906 --> 00:04:46,884
It's so soothing.

79
00:04:46,884 --> 00:04:49,612
I can hardly keep my eyes open.

80
00:04:49,612 --> 00:04:54,818
If only we could bottle the fresh air.

81
00:04:54,818 --> 00:04:59,296
Wouldn't it be wonderful?

82
00:04:59,296 --> 00:05:03,752
We could call it "Deep Sleep Country Air."

83
00:05:03,752 --> 00:05:09,708
It puts you to sleep.

84
00:05:09,708 --> 00:05:15,664
So does the sound.

85
00:05:15,664 --> 00:05:19,042
I've been having a hard time keeping my eyes open

86
00:05:19,042 --> 00:05:21,620
just listening to it.

87
00:05:21,620 --> 00:05:27,576
It's like a special music.

88
00:05:27,576 --> 00:05:30,554
Too bad we can't bottle the sound.

89
00:05:30,554 --> 00:05:33,532
But we can!

90
00:05:33,532 --> 00:05:35,532
Can what?

91
00:05:35,532 --> 00:05:37,009
Bottle the sound.

92
00:05:37,009 --> 00:05:42,465
What are you talking about?

93
00:05:42,465 --> 00:05:46,110
Oh, yeah?

94
00:05:46,110 --> 00:05:47,443
Great idea!

95
00:05:47,443 --> 00:05:50,443
Let's do it!
